# Autonomous Delivery System: Operation Schema

| Id | Operation | Pre-condition | Input | Post-condition |
|----|-----------|---------------|-------|----------------|
| OP-01 | Receive Delivery Request | System is online and the request intake service is accepting connections; the requester is authenticated or holds a valid guest session token. | `customerId`, `pickupLocation`, `destinationLocation`, `packageDetails` (weight, dimensions, fragility flag), `deliveryPriority` | A `DeliveryRequest` record is created with a unique `requestId` and status = `RECEIVED`; the request is persisted and queued for validation; an acknowledgment containing `requestId` is returned to the customer. |
| OP-02 | Validate Order Details | A `DeliveryRequest` with status = `RECEIVED` exists; the address-verification and geocoding service is reachable; service rules and route constraint data are loaded. | `requestId`, `packageDetails`, `pickupLocation`, `destinationLocation`, `serviceAreaBoundary`, `payloadLimits`, `routeConstraints` | If all checks pass (item information complete, addresses geocoded and accurate, locations within the service area, route constraints satisfied, service rules met), status = `VALIDATED`. Otherwise, status = `REJECTED`, a rejection reason code is recorded, and the customer is notified. No vehicle is reserved. |
| OP-03 | Assign Delivery Task | A `DeliveryRequest` with status = `VALIDATED` exists; the fleet management service is reachable; at least one vehicle is registered in the fleet. | `requestId`, `pickupLocation`, `packageDetails`, `deliveryPriority`, `fleetStatusSnapshot`, `selectionCriteria` (proximity, battery level, payload capacity) | Exactly one available vehicle (status = `IDLE`, no active faults) is selected; vehicle status changes `IDLE` to `ASSIGNED` as an atomic operation to prevent double assignment; a mission record `(requestId, vehicleId)` is persisted; request status = `ASSIGNED`. If no vehicle is available, status = `PENDING_VEHICLE` and the request is queued for retry. |
| OP-04 | Pre-Trip System Check | Vehicle status = `ASSIGNED`; the vehicle is powered on and docked at the base or loading station; the diagnostics interface is responsive. | `vehicleId`, `sensorDiagnostics` (LiDAR, camera, ultrasonic, GPS, IMU), `batteryLevel`, `navigationModuleStatus`, `safetySystemStatus`, `minimumBatteryThreshold` | If all subsystems pass and the battery level meets `minimumBatteryThreshold`, `preTripCheckResult` = `PASS` and vehicle status = `READY`. If any check fails, `preTripCheckResult` = `FAIL`, vehicle status = `FAULT`, the failure is logged, and the mission is returned to OP-03 for reassignment. |
| OP-05 | Load Cargo | Vehicle status = `READY`; the vehicle is stationary at the loading station; the cargo bay is empty and unlocked; the package is present at the loading point. | `vehicleId`, `requestId`, `packageId`, `packageWeight`, `loadingStationId` | The package is placed in the cargo bay in a secure and balanced position; the measured weight matches `packageWeight` within tolerance; the cargo bay is locked; a release credential is generated and bound to `requestId`; vehicle status = `LOADED`; request status = `LOADED`. |
| OP-06 | Initialize Navigation Plan | Vehicle status = `LOADED`; the cargo bay is locked; current map, traffic, and restriction data are available to the routing engine. | `vehicleId`, `currentPosition`, `destinationLocation`, `mapData`, `trafficData`, `restrictedZones`, `batteryLevel`, `optimizationObjective` (shortest time or lowest energy) | A route is generated as an ordered list of waypoints from `currentPosition` to `destinationLocation`; the route avoids restricted zones; estimated energy use is below available battery minus a safety reserve; the ETA is calculated and stored in the route plan; request status = `ROUTE_PLANNED`. If no feasible route exists, status = `ROUTE_FAILED`, the vehicle is released to `IDLE`, and the incident is logged. |
| OP-07 | Begin Vehicle Movement | A feasible route plan exists; vehicle status = `LOADED`; the departure path is clear; the localization system reports a valid position fix. | `vehicleId`, `routePlan`, `ETA`, `preTripCheckResult` | The route plan is loaded into the vehicle's navigation controller; the vehicle transitions from idle mode to active transit and leaves the base; vehicle status = `IN_TRANSIT`; request status = `DISPATCHED`; the departure timestamp is recorded; the customer receives the ETA. |
| OP-08 | Monitor Road Conditions | Vehicle status = `IN_TRANSIT`; perception sensors report a healthy status; the telemetry link to the control center is active. | `sensorStream` (LiDAR, camera, ultrasonic), `trafficSignalState`, `lanePosition`, `environmentalData` (weather, visibility, surface condition), `safetyDistanceThreshold`, `telemetryInterval` | Obstacles, traffic signals, lane position, and environmental changes are detected, classified, and located. When an obstacle lies within `safetyDistanceThreshold`, a hazard event is raised to the navigation controller. Telemetry is transmitted at every `telemetryInterval`; a threshold breach raises an alert and sets vehicle status = `FAULT` or `RETURNING` according to severity. All events are logged with timestamps. |
| OP-09 | Navigate to Destination | Vehicle status = `IN_TRANSIT`; the route plan is active; the monitoring output from OP-08 is available to the navigation controller. | `vehicleId`, `routePlan`, `currentPosition`, `currentHeading`, `speedLimits`, `hazardEvents`, `waypointIndex` | The vehicle follows the waypoints in order, adjusting steering, speed, and pathing; speed stays at or below the limit and lateral deviation stays within the corridor tolerance; a controlled stop or avoidance maneuver is executed on hazard events; a replan is requested if the path stays blocked; `waypointIndex` is updated at each waypoint; the operation ends with the vehicle within the arrival radius of the drop-off point. |
| OP-10 | Deliver Package | Vehicle status = `IN_TRANSIT`; the vehicle is within the arrival radius of `destinationLocation`; a safe stopping position is available; the cargo bay is locked. | `vehicleId`, `requestId`, `currentPosition`, `destinationLocation`, `arrivalRadius`, `recipientCredential`, `expectedCredential`, `maxAttempts`, `recipientWaitTimeout` | The vehicle stops at a safe position and applies its parking brake; vehicle status = `ARRIVED`. If the recipient credential matches `expectedCredential`, the cargo bay unlocks, the package removal is confirmed by weight or door sensor, the bay is relocked, and request status = `DELIVERED`. If authentication fails `maxAttempts` times or the timeout expires, the bay stays locked, request status = `DELIVERY_FAILED`, and the package is retained for the return trip. |
| OP-11 | Update Delivery Status | Request status is `DELIVERED` or `DELIVERY_FAILED`; the order management service and control system are reachable. | `requestId`, `vehicleId`, `finalDeliveryStatus`, `deliveryTimestamp`, `failureReason` (if applicable), `proofOfDelivery` | The final order status, timestamps, and proof-of-delivery record are persisted; the completion event is communicated to the control system or operator; the customer receives a final confirmation or failure notice; the mission record is marked complete. |
| OP-12 | Return to Base | Delivery status has been recorded (OP-11); the cargo bay is locked; the battery level is sufficient for the return route. | `vehicleId`, `baseLocation`, `returnRoute`, `batteryLevel`, `chargingThreshold` | The vehicle travels to `baseLocation` and docks; vehicle status = `RETURNING` during the trip, then `IDLE` after docking; the vehicle is queued for charging if the battery level is below `chargingThreshold`; a post-mission system check confirms readiness for the next task; the assignment record is closed. |
